# Play test of Highmoor Lodge (CIPlay highmoor_lodge, in a test world 'CI ...'). Points as in its recipe ("offset").
# The lodge on the north shelf (floor 3.45 m, its front door at 4.75 33, the upper floor 5.97 m), the kitchen behind it,
# the ballroom on its west side, the boiler house behind the ballroom (its door at 2.25 25); the jetty on the north beach;
# the hedge maze on the west lowland (floor 4.55 m, the way in at -28 10, the heart at -26 -2).
island Highmoor Lodge
offset -0.6789 -0.0309
expect step 0
expect title The Winter Book
wait 5
expect animals Goat 2
expect animals Dolphin 2

# Off the jetty and up the drive to the lodge's door
walk 1.5 49 to 1.5 42 to 3.5 38 to 4.75 35.5 h=3.4
zone lodge
expect step 0

# The lobby: the ledger on the front desk (a page), page two beside it; the lounge's typewriter, page one
walk 4.75 35.5 to 4.75 32 to 5 30.6 h=3.45 below=5.5
read Manager's ledger
expect step 1
read Typed page, chapter four
read Typed page, chapter one

# Up the stair along the lounge's left wall (its foot at the back) to the landing at the front, round to room 9 behind the
# partition upstairs: page three on the bed
walk 5 30.6 to 8 29 to 9.25 28.1 h=3.45 below=5.5
walk 9.25 28.1 to 9.25 31.9 to 7.75 32.1 to 6.6 30.75 to 4.6 30.75 to 2.8 29.6 h=5.97 below=8.5
read Typed page, chapter nine

# Back down; through the back into the kitchen (page four, two rats); through the lobby's side into the ballroom (page five)
# (down to the stair's foot first, then on: the walker turned for 8 29 a step above the foot now and then and met the
# landing's floor - the SL6 plan runs, 2026-10-19)
walk 4.6 30.75 to 6.6 30.75 to 7.75 32.1 to 9.25 31.9 to 9.25 28.1 h=3.45 below=8.5
walk 9.25 28.1 to 8 29 h=3.45 below=5.5
walk 8 29 to 7.75 28.3 to 7.75 26 to 7.6 24.6 h=3.45 below=5.5
read Typed page, chapter eleven
walk 7.75 26 to 7.75 28.6 to 3 30.75 to 1.5 30.75 to -1 30.75 h=3.45 below=5.5
read Typed page, chapter twelve
expect step 2
# Out of the front door, round the ballroom to the maze on the west lowland; through its turns to the heart
walk -1 30.75 to 3 30.75 to 4.75 32 to 4.75 35.5 h=3.45 below=5.5
walk 4.75 35.5 to -9 35 to -12 20 to -28 13.5 h=4.5
zone maze
expect step 3
walk -28 13 to -28 8 to -36 8 to -36 -8 to -28 -8 to -28 -4 h=4.55
zone mazeheart
kill Polar bear
expect step 4
open Caretaker's coat
expect story boilerkey 1
expect step 5

# Back to the boiler house behind the ballroom: the key slides its door aside; the valves - the wrong one first
walk -28 -4 to -28 -8 to -36 -8 to -36 8 to -28 8 to -28 13 h=4.55
walk -28 13.5 to -12 20 to -9 26 to 1.4 26 h=3.45
use boilerdoor
expect message slides aside on heat and noise
wait 2
walk 1.4 26 to 1.6 24.4 h=3.45 below=5.5
zone boilerroom
expect step 6
use valvebrass
expect message Wrong valve
use valvered
use valvebrass
use valveblack
expect message the boiler falls quiet
expect hidden ballroommusic
open Caretaker's strongbox
wait 2
expect done

# (the pantry, the jetty and shed boxes and the barrel off the jetty have no note on purpose - a note would be a page for
# step 2 - so the play runner, which opens chests by their note's title, leaves them)
